<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    This addon defines no types of its own - the subscription types live in adyensubscriptionconnector,
    which owns them.

    The file exists anyway, and must, because extensioninfo.xml declares a generated coremodule. Without
    an items.xml nothing is generated, so the Manager class named there is never produced and the platform
    refuses to load the extension at startup with

        ClassNotFoundException: com.adyen.commerce.subscription.jalo.Adyensubscriptionb2caddonManager

    That failure does not break the build - it surfaces only when the extension is loaded - and its
    symptom is not an error page but a quiet one: the CMS page still renders, because the page and its
    slots are data, and the JSP still renders, because addoninstall copied it into the storefront. Only
    the controller is missing, so the page comes up empty with nothing in the log to say why.
-->
<items xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="items.xsd">
</items>
